  "protocol_amendment_justification": "Protocol Amendment ADR-005 Section 11: The design-stage disparity target effect was revised from -1.00 pp to -2.00 pp based on reproducible empirical development benchmarks from the Common Voice 27 development pool (reports/stage6m/cv27_development_speaker_benchmarks.csv, N=96 speakers across 6 canonical strata, validated for nonnegative error counts and mathematical consistency). High-WER Irish English demonstrated -4.50 pp empirical WER reduction, while low-WER US English demonstrated -2.50 pp, yielding an empirical disparity contraction of Delta_D = -2.00 pp with mean shift of -3.45 pp. Note on Confirmatory Power: Under the word-weighted paired cluster inference model with Bonferroni 99.444th percentile bootstrap tail estimation, the candidate design of N=78 speakers per stratum achieves approximately 38-42% joint statistical power under the empirical Delta_D = -2.00 pp effect size, and is therefore classified as UNDERPOWERED. Achieving >= 90% joint statistical power under empirical Delta_D = -2.00 pp requires N >= 160 speakers per stratum (960 confirmatory speakers total); or alternatively, at N=78, requires a prospective design target of Delta_D <= -3.50 pp. Confirmatory Cohort 3 execution remains strictly blocked on HOLD until formal protocol amendment and independent governance approval."
